{"t":1791444197,"office":"LWX","station":"KDCA","point":"38.8894,-77.0352","field":"38.9429,-76.5684","field_station":"KNAK","afd":{"id":"36c5ba3c-d082-4211-b1e6-e66382b9bc96","office":"LWX","issuanceTime":"2026-10-08T05:41:00+00:00","productText":"\n000\nFXUS61 KLWX 080541\nAFDLWX\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Baltimore MD/Washington DC\n141 AM EDT Thu Oct 8 2026\n\n.WHAT HAS CHANGED...\nNothing.\n\n&&\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n- 1) Quiescent weather expected through the end of the week.\n\n- 2) Remnants of Tropical Storm Isaias arrive late this \n     weekend.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Quiescent weather expected through the end of\nthe week.\n\nA dry cold front will move through this morning. Cannot rule out\na rogue shower in the Alleghenies, but the frontal passage is\nexpected to largely be moisture starved. Winds will shift to \nthe W and NW at 10 to 15 mph with gusts of 20 to 25 mph, \nperhaps occasional/peak gusts near 30 mph near higher terrain. \nDespite the passage of the front, downsloping winds likely \npushing temps well into the 70s to near 80 for most. Lowered Tds\ngiven the downsloping setup NBM was not catching at all.\n\nSeasonable (albeit slightly cooler) temps and dry conditions \nwill then persist under high pressure Fri through Fri\nnight. Lowered Tds in aft given recent NBM issues and favorable\nsetup for lower Tds.\n\nHigh pressure retreats off to the NE Sat with cloudcover from\nthe remnants of Isaias moving in and thickening through the day.\nAny precip likely holds off until Sat night or Sun morning. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Remnants of Tropical Storm Isaias arrive late this \nweekend.\n\nTropical Storm Isaias continues to be the main weather feature to \nmonitor over the forecast period with remnants expected to impact \nthe forecast area later this weekend. The National Hurricane Center \nhas TS Isaias tracking a bit slower and further east than previous \nforecasts, with remnant circulation over central Kentucky early \nSun afternoon. Dry conditions are expected for the forecast \narea through Sat, with precip associated with remnants of \nIsaias reaching the forecast area on Sun. The most likely \nimpact to the forecast area continues to be rain although severe\nweather cannot be ruled out on Sunday. Most likely rainfall is\nan inch or two, but still highly uncertain. This many days out,\nthe track, timing, and impacts of Tropical Storm Isaias remain \nuncertain so be sure to monitor hurricanes.gov for the latest \nforecast.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION /06Z THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nWinds shift behind dry cold frontal passage this morning. \nOtherwise, P6SM SKC through 21Z Fri. Then, increasing high \nclouds Fri night.\n\nVFR conditions are expected Sat as high pressure remains \ndominant over the region, though clouds will increase and \nthicken through the day. Winds will be out of the S to SE on \nSat at 5 to 10 knots. \n\nSub-VFR conditions are expected on Sun as remnants associated \nwith Tropical Storm Isaias impact the terminals. Reductions in \nceilings and visibilities are possible during rainfall with \nsouthwest winds gusting around 20 knots. On Mon, VFR conditions\nreturn with northwest winds remaining light. \n\n&&\n\n.MARINE...\nSCA is in effect through about sunrise for the main channel of \nthe Chesapeake Bay up to Pooles Island, the tidal Choptank and \nTangier Sound, and the lower tidal Potomac River as S to \nSW winds gust to around 20 kts. Winds today shift to the W and \nNW with SCA gusts expected over the upper tidal Potomac and \nupper Chesapeake Bay/Baltimore Harbor. Winds drop below SCA by \nlate Thu afternoon through Fri.\n\nWinds are expected to remain below SCA criteria on Sat as high \npressure remains dominant over the region. However, by Sat \nevening, we could see a brief burst of S'ly channeling winds \nthat come close to criteria. Confidence is low at this time. \n\nSmall Craft Advisory criteria winds are likely on Sun with \nwinds gusting around 20 knots as the remnants of Isaias move \nthrough. Winds diminish on Mon, blowing around 10 knots out of \nthe NW. \n\n\n&&\n\n.TIDES/COASTAL FLOODING...\nAction stage at a few sensitive sites this morning given\nelevated anomalies. Otherwise, tide levels may increase during \nthe second half of the weekend depending on the exact direction \nand strength of the winds as the remnants of Isaias approach.\n\n&&\n\n.LWX WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...\nDC...None.\nMD...Small Craft Advisory from 6 AM this morning to 6 PM EDT this \n     evening for MDZ008.\nVA...None.\nWV...None.\nMARINE...Small Craft Advisory from 6 AM this morning to 6 PM EDT this \n     evening for ANZ530-535-538.\n     Small Craft Advisory until 6 PM EDT this evening for ANZ531.\n     Small Craft Advisory until 6 AM EDT early this morning for \n     ANZ532-533-537-541.\n     Small Craft Advisory until 8 AM EDT this morning for ANZ534-\n     543.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...AVS/CPB\nAVIATION...AVS/CPB\nMARINE...AVS/CPB\n"},"forecast":{"t":1791444164,"days":{"2026-10-08":{"hi":78,"lo":53,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-09":{"hi":74,"lo":55,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-10":{"hi":73,"lo":59,"pop":30,"short":"Partly Sunny"},"2026-10-11":{"hi":68,"lo":63,"pop":87,"short":"Rain Showers"},"2026-10-12":{"hi":72,"lo":61,"pop":42,"short":"Chance Rain Showers"},"2026-10-13":{"hi":74,"lo":54,"pop":15,"short":"Mostly Sunny"},"2026-10-14":{"hi":64,"lo":null,"pop":7,"short":"Sunny"}}},"grid":{"t0":1791442800,"n":48,"ceil":[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],"vis":[10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.